 7	\title{Exact Periods and Labelled Orbit Counts for Closed Pointer Reversal}
 8	\author{Anonymous}
 9	\date{}
10	\begin{document}
11	\maketitle
12	\begin{abstract}
13	The familiar pointer-reversal assignment becomes a finite permutation when
14	both registers and every stored pointer range over the same finite label set,
15	with no sentinel or stopping rule. We classify its orbits on the full carrier.
16	The active augmented-edge two-core is a figure-eight, barbell or theta, while
17	all complementary pointers remain fixed. Explicit branch return states give
18	seven exact-period cases, including loops and indistinguishable parallel
19	edges. On $n\ge2$ labels the attained periods are precisely
20	$\{1,\ldots,2n\}\cup\{2n+2,2n+4,\ldots,4n-4\}$.
21	Observable orientation and order decorations then give an explicit rational
22	bivariate core generating function and a labelled orbit census after arbitrary
23	frozen complements are attached. We distinguish these closed-carrier results
24	from the established reversal kernel, initialized-list analyses and
25	fixed-digraph rotor theorems.
26	\end{abstract}
